## Statuses

Configured statuses:
{{range .Statuses}}
- **{{.Name}}**{{if .Description}}: {{.Description}}{{end}}
{{- end}}

**`deferred` = parked**: intentionally not-now but not abandoned. Non-terminal, not archived (stays visible in listings), but **excluded from `nibs list --ready`**. Choosing among the not-active states: **draft** = needs refinement before it can be worked; **deferred** = ready but parked for later; **scrapped** = will not be done (terminal, archived). `deferred` is a status, not a priority.

**Status filtering (`nibs list` / `nibs rel`) is open by default.** With no status flag both commands list only **open** nibs (completed and scrapped hidden), and the header discloses how many were hidden — `# 12 nibs (3 hidden: completed/scrapped — --all to include)`. `-s`/`--status` and `--no-status` accept status **groups** as well as concrete statuses:
- **open** = in-progress, todo, draft, deferred (every non-archived status)
- **closed** = completed, scrapped (the archived statuses)
- **parked** = deferred

An explicit `-s` overrides the open default (`-s closed` shows only completed/scrapped); `--all` includes every status; `--open`/`--active` is shorthand for `-s open`. So **open work under a parent needs no post-filtering** — `nibs rel <id> --rel descendants -t bug` already returns only open bugs; don't hand-roll a `--json | python` status filter. `-c`/`-q` honor the open default too; add `--all` for true totals. (A filter that admits no status, e.g. `--no-status open`, is a validation error rather than a silent empty result.)

